{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For the sake of.</b> All this greatness I do not do for your sake, but for Israel's sake, that you may send the exile and also rebuild Jerusalem." "<b>I call you.</b> Like אֶקְרָא בְשִׁמְךָ לִי אַתָּה (Isaiah 43:1)." "<b>and you did not know Me.</b> For He does not yet speak to the created being."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:06.404735497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}